Next was Mojo (of course).  

Third artifact was Wallet of Perseus via saccing.  Excellent choice!!

Then Grayswandir.  Looted from a Dwarf King no less.  I used that for 
quite some time off handed with Mojo, and it was good.

Ended up getting Whisperfeet and Deluder on the sac routine.  Quite nice!

I was in a rut though.  I had cloned zorkmids at every shop I found...I 
had over 65,000 credits at one...IDing items was NO problem!  A pet fire 
elemental killed the cross-aligned Priest in Minetown.  Bummer about that 
too because he was the ONLY priest in the entire game (other than the 
Moloch guys, and they didn't respond to Taming scrolls).  But I did get 6 
points of AC protection before he was greased.  

So here I was with all items IDed, and goads of credits but just was not 
advancing.  Had teleportitis but no control...that was bad especially 
since I was near the Chaotic quest portal.  I had to do and redo levels 8 
to 15 three times.  I got so bored with it that I totally mined out 
levels three and five with nothing more than a pick axe.  

I finally got TP control!  Yippee!  Picked up the Orb of Knowldege from 
the Quest, but never really used it because I got really lucky in that 
Rings of Warning, Searching, Stealth, Protection AND Increase to hit were 
ALL edible as a Xorn!  Let's hear it for cool intrinsics!!  Oh yea, I 
gained Magic Breathing from a tasty amulet I found as well.

Then once I got to One-Eyed Sam's things started looking up.  It is 
amazing how much stuff you can jam into a Wallet of Perseus.  8o)

Set up a base camp at 23 and 29.  Did the Neutral quest.  Got a genocide 
and did the Lawful quest (minus dwarves, mind flayers and their ilk).

Later on I got Magicbane from a sac-fest with 4 WoMS...so I tried my hand 
