The other two deaths were in the Castle.  There was a Titan at the far 
side of the inner court and I ran to him but got surrounded before I 
could toss an egg his way.  Went down from HP loss and then later from a 
sickness I got (no idea how).  2 more AoLS burned up.

Just as I was ready to go for the Book of the Dead, I decided to dig out 
trenches from the stairs up to the stairs down on every level from 1 to 
the Castle.  It took a LONG time, but was worth it because when I was 
running away with the AoY, I would get swarmed by monsters...well all I 
had to do was dispatch what was directly in front of me because the rest 
of them were stuck in pits!  It also laid out the direct route to the 
next stairs as well.

While I was fooling around with pit digging I prayed and got to be the 
Envoy of Balance.  Gained the Vorpal Blade, which I enchanted.  
+7 Mojo, +1 Magicbane, and +7 Vorpy.  Sweet.  I did about ten or so 
sacrifices and lo and behold, I got a feeling of reconciliation!!  So I 
was the Envoy who could safely pray!  Hey it was a new one for me, OK?

Anyway I got the book, egged Rodney 13 times.  Got the AoY after egging 
the High Priest of Moloch and his clean up crew (I went into the Temple 
with 132 cockatrice eggs, came out with 102).

On the way up to Level 1 with the AoY, I killed a Hill Giant who was 
carrying (and NO I am not making this up) 1337 zorkmids!!  Even though I 
had long ago stopped picking up gold (had over 100,000 in a chest at base 
camp #1), I HAD to accept this as a sign.  I pocketed the loot and on my 
way I went, somehow feeling that I was now destined to ascend.

Got to the Planes.  Made a beeline for that Portal on Earth with one of 
the 20 Wands of Digging I took.  I tossed those once I got to Air of 
course.  Took off the AoLS in Air so I could fly.  There were ZERO 
summoning types in Air.  THAT amazed me!!  Fire and water were totally 
uneventful; I made right for the portals and got to them quickly and 
easily.

The Astral Plane gave me the willies.  I was afraid to take a single 
step.  Finally after a bit I found the middle room.  Pestilence tried to 
keep me out...he nearly succeeded.  I killed him once with the help of my 
unicorn horn and several !oFH that I drank/threw at him.  He came back as 
I was killing the last of his summoned help, so I TPed him away.  I ran 
into the room and egged everything in my path.  Silly me.  Turns out it 
was the Neutral Room and I had just egged a Priest of Odin AND the High 
Priest of Odin.  There was now a really mad Angel nearby.  I am surprised 
that reward pet Angel didn't turn on me!

So I lost telepathy, gained a LARGE amount of Bad Luck(tm) and could no 
longer safely pray.  But I was standing on the Altar to Odin holding the 
Amulet of Yendor.  Nuff said, you know the rest.

The one thing that amazed me most was that through all that, I only saw 
and killed ONE Archon.  Not complaining mind you...it was just 
surprising.

